@@ -56,47 +56,8 @@ integration. Browser app + PWA-installable on iOS/Android.
 
 Detailed steps in `DEPLOYMENT.md`.
 
-## Rolling change analysis
+## Rolling Change Analysis
 
-Uses the Positions ticker catalogue/search and accepts full Bloomberg tickers.
-Paste comma/newline-separated full tickers to add a list, then Analyze once.
-Prices already loaded into the shared HISTORY dataset are shown immediately; new
-observations are merged back without replacing other tickers or older dates.
-Other tabs retain their current request/refresh behavior.
-Settings use the existing shared desk store; localStorage is only its mirror.
-
-Daily PX_LAST observations are saved in `daily_prices` and coverage metadata in
-`daily_price_coverage`, inside the existing `risk_system.db` and its backup flow.
-Existing `bbg_history_cache.json` and `bbg_field_history__PX_LAST.json` seed missing
-history; newer snapshot revisions can correct older observations. New prices merge into the shared
-history cache for other tabs. Live quote snapshots are not historical series.
-
-`GET /api/bbg-history?range=1&tickers=...&from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD`
-uses the existing shared history route and returns saved prices immediately and a job identifier when gaps need filling.
-Poll with the same query plus `job`. Failed/partial fetches retain saved values
-and return warnings. Gap fetches use the configured Bloomberg data-agent BDH
-client, explicit dates and batches of12, with duplicate work suppressed. Empty
-or partial historical responses retry after six hours; current-day coverage
-retries after five minutes. Provisional prices are finalized after the session.
-Fully observed historical intervals persist. Provider availability is not required for cached
-coverage. A whole-series refresh is not forced by Analyze.
-
-One browser request accepts100 tickers; larger selections are split automatically.
-All covers2600 calendar days. Custom ranges plus lookback may span up to4000
-calendar days. Rolling calculations use calendar periods, month-end clamping and
-the previous available observation. Null prices remain gaps; explicit zero prices
-are retained, but cannot serve as percentage-return denominators.
-
-Validation (isolated, no live Bloomberg):
-- `python -m pytest tests/test_rolling_cache.py -q`
-- `node tests/test_rolling_change.js` with Playwright and Edge available.
-
-The Rolling change summary shows 1M, 3M, 6M and 12M price changes for each ticker.
-Percentiles use valid daily rolling changes within the selected date range, with
-average ranks for ties (0-100); fewer than two observations show a dash. Red marks
-the bottom decile, green the top decile. The table follows the %/absolute mode
-and end date. Shared history requests include a one-year lookback for the table.
-
-Rolling requests also include the preceding available close at the earliest
-lookback boundary. Missing predecessor coverage uses the same database gap
-planner, expanding up to 4,000 days; missing prices remain unavailable.
+Rolling Analysis has moved to its standalone repository:
+https://github.com/vascovalla/Rolling-Change-Analysis-
+Existing saved Risk prices and database history are preserved.
